              This mirrors every prior W7 page in apps/parity/windows-ledger.json, e.g. the sibling
              SignalLogViewerPage and SignalsWorkspacePage.)

Shape of the parity unit (apps/parity/parity-manifest.json id=page:telemetry/SignalExplorer)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
requiredCount=20 = 1 panel (GlassPanel1) + 4 data-states + 15 strings. 0 charts, 0 maps. Data source (1):
useSignals (GET /signals/{vehicleId}/available). The web page composes the shared telemetry components
(SignalSelector, SignalStatsPanel, SignalChartPanel + the SignalHistoryTable region) inside a
PageContainer with an Explore/Live workspace; the native port reproduces the whole tree and composes the
already-ported shared surfaces rather than re-implementing them.

Native realisation (Fluent / WinUI 3, ADR-002/004/005/006/011/013/014/015)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
- SignalExplorerPage : UserControl — the page header (PageTitle / Subhead, the vehicle TsSelect and the
  live-connection TsBadge), the load-failed TsAlertBanner (web anyError = signalsError ?? historicalError),
  the no-vehicle TsEmptyState, the explore-controls TsGlassPanel (GlassPanel1 — the shared SignalSelector
  capped at 5, the TsRangePicker time-range, the Per Page TsSelect, the Explore TsButton, the Live TsButton
  and the live TsHelpTooltip), the pre-explore TsEmptyState, and the results region (the shared
  SignalStatsPanel + SignalChartPanel the subtitle promises, plus the SignalHistoryTable port — TsTableSkeleton
  / TsDataTable / no-data TsEmptyState). Thin renderer: every label/value/visibility flows from
  SignalExplorerDisplay; PropertyChanged is marshalled onto the UI thread; tokens only (no literal colours).
  Exposes UpdateLiveState (the P1/S4 SSE seam feeding the connection badge).
- SignalExplorerPageViewModel : INotifyPropertyChanged — UI-thread-free state holder. Owns the URL-equivalent
  state (vehicle, signals, range, per-page) + the latched exploreKey and the Live toggle, reads the fleet +
  per-vehicle available catalogue through ISignalExplorerFeed, runs the deferred Explore history fetch
  (one GET /signals/{id}/{signal}/history per signal), and projects SignalExplorerDisplay. LoadAsync /
  SelectVehicleAsync (wipes explored, web useEffect(()=>setExploreKey(null),[vehicleId])) / SetSelectedSignals
  (caps at 5) / SetRange / SetPerPage / ExploreAsync / ToggleLive / UpdateLiveState; superseding CTS; no I/O in the view.
- SignalExplorerProjection / SignalExplorerModel / SignalExplorerDisplay — pure projection (no WinUI types)
  resolving all 15 i18n keys on every call (the conditionally-rendered Live keys are pre-resolved so a single
  projection requests the whole manifest set), the historicalStats (min/max/avg/count) and chartData
  (timestamp-pivoted SignalChartSample) memos, the history-table rows, and the catalog data-state flags.
  SignalExplorerRegistration — RouteName="SignalExplorer" (matches RouteTable.cs
  Page("SignalExplorer","signal-explorer",TelemetrySignals)), the three generated operation ids and the
  PerPage choices. PII-safe SignalExplorerDiagnostics (view.opened only).
- ISignalExplorerFeed / EmptySignalExplorerFeed (no-backend default the shell-registered page mounts against) /
  SignalExplorerClientFeed (the generated-OpenAPI-client adapter, ADR-004) binding GET /vehicles,
  GET /signals/{vehicleID}/available and GET /signals/{vehicleID}/{signalName}/history with snake_case
  from/to/limit query (never camelCase, never a double /api/v1 prefix).
- Shell registration: apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs registers
  PageFactory.Register("SignalExplorer", () => new FeatureViews.Telemetry.SignalExplorerPage()).

i18n note (ADR-014)
-------------------
The 15 manifest keys are resolved through keyed ILocalizer.GetString(key, <web default>) flowing through
ShellLocalizer -> shell Localization (resw lookup -> English fallback), exactly as the web resolves the inline
t(key, default) fallbacks. Zero hardcoded literals; the auto-generated resw is left untouched.

